# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same values in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for production.
#
# .env* is gitignored (this template is the only exception). Nothing
# here is prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, so no value is inlined into the client
# bundle. src/lib/deliverInquiry.ts is marked `server-only`, so these
# are unreachable from client components by construction.

# ── Contact form delivery ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Modes are tried in this order: SMTP → Resend → webhook → server log.
# If none is configured, inquiries are logged rather than lost.

# 1. SMTP (Hostinger) — the active setup.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.hostinger.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=support@harizx.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=support@harizx.com

# 2. Resend — alternative HTTP transport. Ignored while SMTP is set.
#    Sender must be on a domain verified in Resend; use the
#    send.harizx.com subdomain so its DNS records don't collide with
#    the Hostinger mail records on the root domain.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# CONTACT_FROM="HarizX Site <site@send.harizx.com>"

# 3. Webhook — posts the inquiry as JSON (Slack, Zapier, a CRM).
#    Ignored while SMTP or Resend is set. Leave blank if unused.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=


# ── Email agent (drafts replies, never sends) ───────────────────────
# Reads support@harizx.com over IMAP, drafts a reply with Claude, and
# saves it to Drafts for review. See src/lib/emailAgent/.

# Same mailbox and password as SMTP above. Falls back to SMTP_USER /
# SMTP_PASSWORD if these are unset, so you need only set the host.
IMAP_HOST=imap.hostinger.com
IMAP_PORT=993
# IMAP_USER=support@harizx.com
# IMAP_PASSWORD=

# Hostinger's drafts folder. Change only if your webmail names it
# differently (some servers use plain "Drafts").
IMAP_DRAFTS_MAILBOX=INBOX.Drafts

# ── Which model drafts the replies ──────────────────────────────────
# Set ONE. Whichever key is present is used; AGENT_PROVIDER forces a
# choice if both are set.
#
# PRIVACY: free tiers train on what you send them, and these emails
# contain customer names, companies and project details. Google's free
# Gemini tier does this; paid tiers of either provider do not. Pick
# with that in mind.

# Free tier — aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Paid, not used for training — console.anthropic.com
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional tuning
# AGENT_PROVIDER=gemini          # or: anthropic
# AGENT_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash   # or: claude-sonnet-5
# AGENT_BATCH_SIZE=5


# ── Site chatbot ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reuses GEMINI_API_KEY above — no extra key needed. The widget hides
# itself and the endpoint returns 503 if that key is unset.
#
# This endpoint is PUBLIC, so every call spends model quota. It is rate
# limited per IP and caps message length, history depth and output
# tokens. The counter is per serverless instance, so on Vercel the real
# ceiling is (instances × limit) — move it to Upstash/Vercel KV if the
# free tier ever gets exhausted.

# CHAT_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# Shared secret protecting the cron endpoint. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Vercel Cron sends it automatically as a Bearer token.
CRON_SECRET=
